  "article": [
    {
      "level": 2,
      "heading": "Overview",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "Use the `intersection()` function in the expression of a matchmaking rule to find the common items in arrays. For example, intersection `([[ ‘a’, ‘b’ ], [ ‘b’, ‘c’ ], [ ‘b’, ‘d’]])` returns `[ ‘b’ ]`.",
          "refs": []
        }
      ],
      "listItems": []
    },
    {
      "level": 3,
      "heading": "Declaration",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "```other\narray intersection(array[array[any]] $sets)\n```",
          "refs": []
        }
      ],
      "listItems": []
    },
    {
      "level": 3,
      "heading": "Parameters",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "-`sets`: An array of arrays that the function converts to sets and then intersects with each other.",
          "refs": []
        }
      ],
      "listItems": []
    },
    {
      "level": 3,
      "heading": "Return value",
      "paragraphs": [
        {
          "text": "A set that’s the intersect of the set representation of the arrays in `sets`.",
          "refs": []
        }
      ],
      "listItems": []
    }
  ],
